CaTCHseq pipeline
================

Overview
--------
The CaTCHseq pipeline processes PCR-amplified CaTCH libraries from FASTQ files through mapping, barcode collapsing/deduplication, multiplet handling, and reporting. It is built with Nextflow (DSL2) and supports CellRanger or STARsolo mapping. Deduplication leverages umi_tools network-based clustering with tunable strategies and distances for CaTCH barcodes and UMIs.

Quick start (Docker-based defaults)
-----------------------------------
```bash
nextflow run nextflow/main.nf \
	--libraries <libraries.csv> \
	--outputDir ./CaTCHseq_OUTPUT \
	--reportsDir ./REPORTS
```

Key inputs
----------
- `--libraries` (CSV, required): columns SampleName, Condition, Replicate, LibraryType (GEX|CaTCHseq), R1, R2, CellNumber, Chemistry.
- Reference inputs vary by mapper:
	- CellRanger: `--index` (transcriptome), `--reference`, `--annotation` as needed for building indexes.
	- STARsolo: `--index`, `--reference`, `--annotation`, optional `--whitelist`.

Major parameters
----------------
The authoritative list (including defaults) is `nextflow run nextflow/main.nf --help`; the same set is echoed at the start of every run. The full list:
- Output locations and code paths
	- `--outputDir` (default `./CaTCHseq_nf_OUTPUT`) and `--reportsDir` (default `./REPORTS`).
	- `--scriptDirR`, `--scriptDirPy`, `--binDir`: script/binary paths; keep the defaults (`/tools/scripts/R/`, `/tools/scripts/python/`, `/usr/local/bin/`) when running with Docker, otherwise point them at the checked-out repo.
- General
	- `--mapper` (CellRanger|STAR) and mapper-specific params `--cellranger_params`, `--star_params`, `--idx_params`.
	- `--withQC` to run FastQC/MultiQC; `--fastqc_params` for extra options.
	- `--chunkSize` read chunking for barcode counting.
	- `--minReads` minimum reads per CaTCH barcode; `--filter` to use filtered counts.
	- `--stopOnWarnings` stop the pipeline when a task warns (default true); `--help` prints the usage message.

- Cell calling / CaTCH barcode classification
	- `--min_detected_barcodes` (default 10) minimum CaTCH barcode reads per cell.
	- `--singlet_cutoff` (default 0.8), `--bc1_cutoff` (default 0.4), `--bc2_cutoff` (default 0.3) classify cells as Singlet / Double_Integration.
	- `--stringency` (default|stringent|lenient, default default) fixed-elements filter applied to the raw barcode sequence.

- Barcode/UMI collapsing (umi_tools-backed)
	- Distance cutoffs:
		- `--maxDist` global fallback (default 1).
		- `--maxDistCaTCH` distance for CaTCH barcode collapsing (default 1; falls back to `--maxDist`).
		- `--maxDistUMIs` distance for UMI collapsing (default 1; falls back to `--maxDist`).
	- Network methods:
		- `--clusterMethodCaTCH` (directional/adjacency/cluster, default directional).
		- `--clusterMethodUMIs` (directional/adjacency/cluster, default directional).
	- Uniqueness toggle: `--uniqueCaTCH` (true/false) to enable umi_tools-based collapsing; otherwise Hamming distance.
	- `--majorityVote` (default 90) share of reads the most frequent barcode needs to resolve a multiplet.

- Cell filtering, normalisation and object outputs
	- `--max_mt_percent` (default 10), `--min_detected_features` (default 500), `--hvg_cutoff` (default 0.1) filter cells and call highly variable genes.
	- `--output_seurat` (default true), `--output_sce` (default false), `--output_anndata` (default true) select which single-cell object types are produced and published.
	- `--run_sct` (default false) run SCTransform normalisation and SCT reductions/clustering instead of LogNormalize.
	- `--organism` (Human|Mouse) used for pathway analysis of DE genes; `--marker` RDS file with cell-cycle stage markers.

- CaTCH barcode differential enrichment
	- `--de_method` (barbieq|deseq2, default barbieq) selects the analysis method. `deseq2` runs the legacy DESeq2/edgeR analysis.
	- barbieQ computes per-sample diversity (Shannon/Simpson) and dominance (Simpson's D, Berger-Parker) indices and tests differential barcode proportions of every condition against the reference condition (`--baseline`, default `Day0`; the legacy param name `--refName` is still accepted).
	- `--de_min_count` (default 10, 0 disables) drops barcodes whose summed count within the two contrasted conditions is below the cutoff; applied per comparison.
	- `--de_min_replicates` (default 2) minimum replicates in a condition required to run differential testing.
	- `--de_all_vs_all` additionally tests every condition against every other condition into a separate table.
	- `--de_rds` optional precomputed barbieQ `.rds` to reuse instead of rebuilding the object, needs to be an absolute path accessible from the task.
	- `--pval_cutoff` (default 0.1) and `--lfc_cutoff` (default 1) set the p-value and log-fold-change cutoffs for the DE plots and tables.
	- As before, the barcode DE analysis runs once per sample tag over all its conditions and replicates, and is skipped entirely when fewer than two conditions are present.

Pipeline steps (high level)
---------------------------
1) **QC** (optional): FastQC → MultiQC summaries.
2) **Mapping**: CellRanger count or STARsolo (with chemistry-specific presets).
3) **Barcode counting**: Count CaTCH barcodes in chunks and merge.
4) **Collapse & filter**: Apply distance/method settings to deduplicate CaTCH barcodes and UMIs; remove background.
5) **Multiplet resolution**: Majority-vote based merging of multiplets.
6) **Reports & tables**: Generate CaTCH barcode and cell summaries plus analytics plots.

CLI mapping for collapse script
-------------------------------
- Nextflow params map to `collapseCaTCHbarcodes.py`:
	- `--clusterMethodCaTCH` → `--cluster-method-catch`
	- `--clusterMethodUMIs`  → `--cluster-method-umis`
	- `--maxDist`            → `--maxdist`
	- `--maxDistCaTCH`       → `--maxdist-catch`
	- `--maxDistUMIs`        → `--maxdist-umis`
	- `--uniqueCaTCH`        → `--unique`
	- `--minReads`           → `--minsupport`
- All default to the original behaviour (directional, distance 1) if not set.

Helper scripts
--------------
- Every Python script in `docker/scripts/python/` and every R script in `docker/scripts/R/` (including `docker/scripts/R/optional/`) exposes its own `--help`/usage message listing all accepted options with defaults; run e.g. `collapseCaTCHbarcodes.py --help` or `Rscript preprocessData.R --help`.
- The pipeline invokes these scripts with the option values derived from the Nextflow params listed above, so the Nextflow options are the user-facing interface.

Outputs
-------
- `OUTPUT/Counts/` – intermediate and collapsed `.sclib` libraries and stats.
- `OUTPUT/Reports/` – tables (`*.CaTCHbarcodes`, `*.cells`) and plots.
- `OUTPUT/CellRanger/` or `OUTPUT/STAR/` – mapper-specific outputs.

Tips
----
- Provide chemistry-specific parameters for STARsolo if deviating from 10X presets.
- Ensure `--libraries` paths are accessible where Nextflow executes (local or workdir-mounted in containers).
